# The Trigger Email extension: the thing that actually sends the mail.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why this file exists.
#
# Two Functions queue outbound mail by writing a document to the `mail`
# collection and then stopping: `squareCheckout` (the bookstore confirmation)
# and `formSubmit` (the parish notification and the submitter's copy). Neither
# has a transport. They were written against this extension, which watches the
# collection and delivers whatever it finds.
#
# The extension was never installed. From 2026-09-05:
#
#   $ firebase ext:list --project spsm-database
#   i  extensions: there are no extensions installed on project spsm-database.
#
# So every one of those messages was queued and left. The queued documents are
# intact and carry no `delivery` field at all — the extension stamps
# `delivery.state` the instant it picks a document up, so an absent `delivery`
# is the proof that nothing has ever read the collection. They go out on their
# own once this is installed; nothing needs re-sending by hand.
#
# The extension is configured HERE rather than clicked through the console, so
# the values below are reviewable, and so a reinstall is a command rather than
# a memory of what somebody typed. Install with:
#
#   firebase deploy --only extensions --project spsm-database
#
# There is exactly one thing this file does not carry, because it must not: the
# API key. See SMTP_PASSWORD at the bottom.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- where it watches -------------------------------------------------------

DATABASE=(default)

# us-east1, and this is the trap. The console offers us-central1 by default,
# which is where every HTTP Function in this project runs — but this extension
# is a v2 Firestore TRIGGER, and a v2 Firestore trigger must sit in the
# database's own region or it never fires. spsm-database is us-east1. Same rule
# that puts onGalleryMediaCreated in us-east1 while its siblings are in
# us-central1; see the note above the export in functions/src/index.ts.
#
# A wrong value here does not error. It installs, reports healthy, and silently
# never delivers, which is indistinguishable from the bug this is fixing.
DATABASE_REGION=us-east1
LOCATION=us-east1

# Must match COLLECTIONS.mail in packages/shared/src/collections.ts. Changing
# one without the other puts the queue and its reader in different places.
MAIL_COLLECTION=mail

# --- how it sends -----------------------------------------------------------

AUTH_TYPE=UsernamePassword

# Resend. The username is the literal string `resend` for every account — the
# API key is the password, and it goes in Secret Manager rather than here.
#
# 465 (SMTPS) rather than 587: Google Cloud blocks outbound port 25, and the
# extension's own guidance is 465 for implicit TLS.
SMTP_CONNECTION_URI=smtps://resend@smtp.resend.com:465

# --- what the buyer sees ----------------------------------------------------

# A SUBDOMAIN, and that is not cosmetic. The root domain's SPF record is
#
#   v=spf1 include:spf.protection.outlook.com -all
#
# — a hard fail, listing Microsoft 365 and nothing else, because the church's
# real mail is on M365 (MX is spsmwayland-org.mail.protection.outlook.com).
# Sending from `@spsmwayland.org` through Resend would fail that check on every
# receiving server. The two ways out are to edit the church's live SPF record,
# which risks their actual mail for the sake of a receipt, or to send from a
# subdomain that carries its own SPF and DKIM and leaves the root alone. This
# is the second.
#
# mail.spsmwayland.org has no DNS records of any kind today, so nothing is
# being taken over. The records Resend issues for it are added at Wix — the
# domain's nameservers are ns10/ns11.wixdns.net, not Microsoft's.
#
# `no-reply@` is a local part on a domain we control, not an invented address:
# the subdomain's own SPF and DKIM are what make it deliverable, and no mailbox
# needs to exist behind it. The display name still says who it is from, which
# is the part that matters in a crowded inbox — a bare no-reply@ address with no
# name reads as machine-sent even when it is legitimate.
DEFAULT_FROM=St. Philopater Mercurius & St. Mina Coptic Orthodox Church <no-reply@mail.spsmwayland.org>

# Deliberately empty. This is the no-reply half of the arrangement, and it is a
# decision rather than an unfinished setting.
#
# With no reply-to, a reply goes to DEFAULT_FROM — no-reply@ on a send-only
# subdomain, with no mailbox behind it — and bounces. That is the intent: the
# church does not have to staff an inbox for a receipt. It costs something,
# though, and the cost is paid in the copy rather than here.
#
# The body of every message must therefore never invite a reply. Two things
# enforce that:
#
#   - packages/shared/src/payments/orderEmail.ts opens the closing paragraph
#     with "This address is not monitored." and says "write to" rather than
#     "reply to". There is a unit test on both.
#   - the address it names is `orderEmail` on the `config/bookstore` document
#     (falling back to the PARISH_EMAIL param in functions/.env.spsm-database).
#     While that is blank the copy says "contact the church office" and names
#     nobody — honest, and the reader still has the reference number and the
#     contact form on the site.
#
# Setting this to a real M365 mailbox later is a one-line change and would make
# replies work. If that happens, the "not monitored" sentence in orderEmail.ts
# has to go in the same commit — a no-reply notice on a mailbox that is read is
# the same kind of lie in the other direction.
DEFAULT_REPLY_TO=

# --- retention --------------------------------------------------------------

# Never, which means these documents are kept indefinitely. That is the
# extension's default and it is being left alone rather than chosen: a mail
# document holds a buyer's address and what they bought, so a retention period
# is a privacy decision that belongs in /privacy alongside the rest of them —
# see apps/website/src/app/privacy. Set TTL_EXPIRE_TYPE to `month` or `year`
# and this file becomes the record of that decision.
TTL_EXPIRE_TYPE=never
TTL_EXPIRE_VALUE=1

# --- not used ---------------------------------------------------------------

# No Handlebars templates and no per-user lookup: both builders compose their
# own subject, text and HTML as plain strings — packages/shared/src/payments/
# orderEmail.ts and functions/src/forms/email.ts — and every `to` is a literal
# address rather than a uid.
TEMPLATES_COLLECTION=
USERS_COLLECTION=
TLS_OPTIONS=

# --- the one value that is not here -----------------------------------------
#
# SMTP_PASSWORD is the Resend API key and is declared `type: secret`, so the
# CLI puts it in Secret Manager and prompts for it on the first install. It
# must never be written into this file: this file is committed, and
# `npm run audit:secrets` reads the real values out of .env and fails if it
# finds them in anything git tracks.
